<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10">
            <!-- Header Banner -->
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 bg-dark-gradient text-white p-4 p-md-5 mb-5">
                <span class="badge px-3 py-2 rounded-pill align-self-start mb-3" style="background-color: rgba(224, 184, 126, 0.22); color: #fdf8f0; border: 1px solid #e0b87e;">
                    <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-code me-1" style="color: #e0b87e;"></i> Project Documentation & Technical Specifications
                </span>
                <h1 class="display-5 fw-extrabold mb-3 text-white">BreedVision: Indigenous Bovine Recognition</h1>
                <p class="lead mb-0" style="color: #e2ecd8;">
                    An end-to-end full-stack AI web application built with ASP.NET Core MVC, C#, ONNX Runtime, and SQL Server for real-time identification and phenotypic characterization of Indian cattle and river buffalo breeds.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Project Background & Need -->
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 bg-white mb-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-geo-alt-fill text-danger me-2"></i> Project Significance & Problem Statement</h3>
                <p class="text-secondary">
                    India possesses one of the world's richest reserves of indigenous bovine genetic biodiversity. The Indian Council of Agricultural Research – National Bureau of Animal Genetic Resources (ICAR-NBAGR) registers and tracks indigenous breeds of cattle (<em>Bos indicus</em>) and riverine buffaloes (<em>Bubalus bubalis</em>).
                </p>
                <p class="text-secondary">
                    Accurate identification of indigenous breeds directly impacts breed conservation, selective artificial insemination, livestock insurance verification, and dairy productivity management. However, field officers and rural dairy farmers often lack immediate morphological taxonomy expertise to differentiate closely related zebu or buffalo breeds. <strong>BreedVision</strong> addresses this gap by offering instant, locally executable, and verifiable AI-assisted breed recognition from mobile and digital photographs.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Deep Learning Architecture & Mathematical Pipeline -->
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 bg-white mb-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-4"><i class="bi bi-cpu-fill text-success me-2"></i> Machine Learning Pipeline & Mathematics</h3>
                
                <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-light">
                            <h6 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2"><i class="bi bi-layers-half text-primary me-1"></i> ConvNeXt Deep Vision Backbone</h6>
                            <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                                The core neural network is a state-of-the-art ConvNeXt architecture exported to <strong>Open Neural Network Exchange (ONNX)</strong> format. It receives a standardized RGB tensor $[1, 3, 224, 224]$ and extracts rich multi-scale visual features through depthwise convolutions and inverted bottleneck stages.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-light">
                            <h6 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2"><i class="bi bi-bullseye text-success me-1"></i> 41-Class Classification Head</h6>
                            <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                                The network terminates in a fine-tuned linear classification head outputting raw logit scores $\mathbf{z} \in \mathbb{R}^{41}$ corresponding to 41 distinct indigenous and registered Indian bovine breeds (33 Cattle + 8 Buffalo).
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-light">
                            <h6 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2"><i class="bi bi-calculator-fill text-warning me-1"></i> Calibrated Softmax Distribution</h6>
                            <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                                Probabilistic confidence scores are computed via normalized softmax over all 41 class logits:
                                $$P(\text{Breed}_k) = \frac{e^{z_k}}{\sum_{j=1}^{41} e^{z_j}} \times 100\%$$
                                Top-5 probability ranks are dynamically streamed to the user interface.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <div class="border rounded-3 p-3 h-100 bg-light">
                            <h6 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2"><i class="bi bi-shield-x text-danger me-1"></i> Out-Of-Distribution (OOD) Protection</h6>
                            <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
                                To prevent false certainty on non-livestock, non-bovine, or invalid images, an empirical rejection boundary is enforced: if Top-1 confidence $< 15\%$, the system automatically flags the prediction as <em>Uncertain / Out-of-Distribution Detection</em>.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

